// sptruss.ac -- the truss's analysis (SketchpadTechnicalDesign.md, "The truss"): the force in
// each member of the truss that the Beam, Load, Roller and Fix entries make, found a slice a pass
// in the main loop.
//
// Bank 11, from its first word, alone. Its three entries run with the extend window open and are
// entered by jsp i [X:013]: taInit from the main bank's start, taTick from its loop while the
// constraint solver sleeps, and taRedo from the view module's vwEntry at a change of the
// magnifier's view. They reach the constraint table (bank 9), the point table (bank 3), the
// view's words (bank 12) and the main bank's words through 16-bit addresses, return by jmp i, and
// call nothing outside bank 11.
// Part of sketchpad.am1, included where it stands.
//
// The truss. Its members are the Beam entries' lines, in the table's order. Its joints are the
// members' ends but the fixed points (Fix, pins held both ways), in the order the members first
// name them; a joint that is a Roller's point slides along the roller's axis a, level unless
// Axis set it, and is held across it. A Load entry's line pushes its point A, when that is a
// joint, with ten times the line's length toward B. Every member is a spring of stiffness k, its
// Beam's (tenths in the parameter word, 1.0 unless Stiff set it), so its force (tension
// positive) is k times its stretch along it, and the joints' displacements u are those that
// balance every load. K u = f, K the sum over the members of k c c^T placed at its free ends'
// unknowns, c its coefficients on them, its direction e on a joint's two and e . a on a roller's
// one. A member of 1.0 is not multiplied, so that a truss whose members are all 1.0 gets exactly
// the numbers it would with no stiffnesses at all. The unknowns are each joint's horizontal
// displacement and, but for a roller, its vertical one; a roller's one is its displacement along
// its axis, numbered in the reverse of a breadth-first order of the joints (taPOrd), which keeps
// each row of K short. K is held from each row's first coupled unknown to its diagonal (its
// profile), factored K = L D L^T in place, and solved by substitution, in the floating point of
// spfloat.ac. A pivot D_i not positive, or not over 2^-23 of K's diagonal, is a mechanism, the
// truss's joints free to move with no member stretched; a joint whose members lie on one line is
// one too, its pivot 0. The forces are k e . (u_B - u_A), rounded, a roller's u its unknown times
// a. A level axis's e . a is e_x itself, not a product, so that a truss whose rollers are all
// level gets exactly the numbers it would with no axes at all.
// The profile, the unknowns' words and each member's e are in banks 14 and 15 (sketchpad.am1);
// the map, the axes, the members' coefficients and stiffnesses in bank 13.
//
// The work is done in phases, each a routine reached by jmp i taPhase: the map of the points,
// the joints, the loads, the members' directions, the rollers' axes, the order, the numbering,
// the profile cleared, the assembly, the factorization, the three substitutions and the forces.
// The long ones go a member, a joint or one term of a sum at a time and give up the pass once
// TRUSSMS have passed since it began (taGo), resuming where they stopped. Every TRUSSCHK, and at
// once after Forces was off, the solver awake or a point or instance held, the truss's entries
// and their points are compared with a snapshot of them (taCheck); a change starts the phases
// again from the map. Nothing is computed while Forces is off, the solver awake (the drawing
// moving) or a point or an instance held.
//
// The readouts. The last phase writes a list, roList, in bank 13: each member's force at its
// midpoint and each load's magnitude, ten times its length, at its line's, at the labels' size,
// centered and kept inside the screen, placed through the magnifier's view and left out when the
// midpoint is off the screen (a change of view writes the list again, taRedo); with no answer,
// three dashes for each, and UNSTABLE under the bar's right, its first word a halt while the
// tape's word is shown there (roGate). penISR starts the list at the frame's closing halt while
// roOn is set and no list is open, and the list's halt ends the frame. roOn is cleared whenever
// the readouts would be stale (taTick away, or the truss changed) and set again once the list
// holds the truss as it is (roOK); the list is written only once a frame has ended since it was
// cleared, so that the display is never in it while it is written. In Stiff mode, Forces on or
// off, the same list shows each member's stiffness in place of its force and no load's
// (TASTIFF), written as the forces' are when the truss's snapshot changes; no analysis runs
// meanwhile, and a change of view starts the truss again (taView).

// The results, which the readouts read: the state (TANONE, no Beam; TABUSY; TAOK; TABAD, no
// answer), set once the readouts are written, why there is none (TAWMECH to
// TAWMANY), a count of the analyses finished, the unknowns and the profile's entries of the
// last (0 when it ended before numbering them), and the members' and joints' counts.
taState, 0
taWhy, 0
taGen, 0
taNU, 0
taNP, 0
taNM, 0
taNJ, 0

// Per member, in the table's order: its force, its points A and B, and the addresses of its
// ends' taUX words (the zero slot's for a pin).
taF,
    table NCON, 0
taMA,
    table NCON, 0
taMB,
    table NCON, 0
taJA,
    table NCON, 0
taJB,
    table NCON, 0

// Per joint: its loads in the load's units, horizontal (taFX) and, TANJ words after, vertical
// (taFY), and whether it is a roller (taJR), 0 or its Roller entry's address complemented.
taFX,
    table TANJ, 0
taFY,
    table TANJ, 0
taJR,
    table TANJ, 0

// Per joint, four tables of TANJ + 1 words, each TANJ + 1 after the one before, a joint's words
// found from its taUX word's address; the last word of each, the zero slot, is a pin's. taUX
// holds the joint's members' count, then its incidences' fill pointer, then (from taPNum) its
// horizontal unknown, or a roller's along its axis; taUY marks it reached in taPOrd, then holds
// its vertical unknown, or -1 for a roller; the zero slot's two hold -1. taJI holds the address
// of its first incidence, and taJN minus its members' count.
taUX,
    table TANJ + 1, 0
taUY,
    table TANJ + 1, 0
taJI,
    table TANJ + 1, 0
taJN,
    table TANJ + 1, 0

// The joints in breadth-first order (taPOrd), each by its taUX word's address.
taOrd,
    table TANJ, 0

// The incidences and the map (taInc, taMap) are in bank 13 (sketchpad.am1), with each member's
// coefficients (tdC). Each roller joint's axis (taAX), and the members' flags of an axis not
// level (taMI) and stiffnesses (taMK), are in bank 3.

// The snapshot taCheck compares, taSnap, is in bank 13 (sketchpad.am1). It holds for each Fix
// and Roller its type and point, a Roller's axis after them
// (taRlD), and for each Beam and Load its type, its points, its parameter word (a Beam's
// stiffness) and its points' places. taSnapE is the full address of the first word past it, 0
// when there is none.
taSnapE, 0

// Numbers of three words (spfloat.ac): zero, which a missing unknown's displacement reads; a
// force's first term; a tenth, made once (taInit), and a member's stiffness (taKOf). The pivot
// being formed and the quotient l of the factorization (taD, taL), 1/L's two inputs (drX, drY)
// and a member's six products (asP1 to asP6, asPrT) are in bank 3.
tdZ,
    0
    0
    0
foT,
    table 3, 0
taTenth,
    table 3, 0
taK,
    table 3, 0

// The phases' state: the main bank's return, the pass's start on the clock, the phase to go on
// with, the last check's time, and nonzero when a check is due at once.
taRtn, 0
taT0, 0
taPhase, 0
taChkAt, 0
taDue, 0

// The analysis' start. No answer and no snapshot, so that the first check builds the truss; no
// readouts, and their list a halt; the forces' view; and a tenth, for the stiffnesses.
// AC and IO are clobbered. Called via jsp i [taInit:013].
taInit,
    dac taRtn
    law TANONE
    dac taState
    dzm taWhy
    dzm taGen
    dzm taNU
    dzm taNP
    dzm taNM
    dzm taNJ
    dzm taSnapE
    dzm i [roOn:0]
    dzm roOK
    dzm roUw
    dzm roSt
    lac i [frameTotal:4]
    dac roHideF
    lac [lpoff halt interrupt]
    dac i [roList:015]
    law 0d10
    jda fInt
    jsp fRcp
    lac [taTenth:013]
    jda faSt
    law 1
    dac taDue
    lac [taIdle:013]
    dac taPhase
    jmp i taRtn

// The main loop's pass. Nothing is done while Forces is off, unless in Stiff mode (taView), or
// while the solver is awake or a point or an instance held. Then the readouts are hidden, and a
// check is due at once. Otherwise UNSTABLE's gate
// follows the tape's word, the truss is checked if one is due (taCheck), started again if it
// changed, or in Stiff mode its stiffnesses written, the readouts shown again if it did not and
// they hold it, and its phase goes on for at most TRUSSMS.
// AC and IO are clobbered. Called via jsp i [taTick:013].
taTick,
    dac taRtn
    rck
    dio taT0
    jsp taView
    lac roSt
    sza                 // skip unless Stiff mode's view
    jmp taOn
    lac i [forcesOn:4]
    sza i               // skip if Forces is on
    jmp taAway
taOn,
    lac i [conWake:4]
    sza                 // skip unless the solver is awake
    jmp taAway
    lac i [dragIdx:4]
    and i [dragInst:4]
    sas [NOPOINT]       // skip unless a point or an instance is held
    jmp taAway
    jsp roGate
    lac taDue
    sza                 // skip unless a check is due at once
    jmp taChk
    lac taT0
    sub taChkAt
    spa                 // skip unless the clock wrapped
    add [CLOCKWRAP]
    sub [TRUSSCHK]
    spa                 // skip once TRUSSCHK have passed since the last check
    jmp i taPhase
taChk,
    dzm taDue
    lac taT0
    dac taChkAt
    jsp taCheck
    sza i               // skip if the truss changed
    jmp taSame
    dzm roOK
    jsp roHide
    lac roSt
    sza                 // skip unless Stiff mode's view
    jmp taStf
    law TABUSY
    dac taState
    dzm taWhy
    jmp taPMap
taStf,
    law TASTIFF
    jmp taFin
taSame,
    lac roOK
    sza                 // skip unless the readouts hold the truss as it is
    dac i [roOn:0]
    jmp i taPhase
taAway,
    law 1
    dac taDue
    jsp roHide
    jmp i taRtn

// Whether the readouts show the stiffnesses (roSt), as in Stiff mode, the constraint mode for
// CTSTIFF. A change either way hides the readouts and drops the snapshot, so that the check, due
// at once, finds the truss changed. The stiffnesses are written, or the analysis that Stiff mode
// cut short starts again. The constraints' marks are made stale too (cMkDirty), so that the main
// loop writes them again (showStep), a Beam's B giving way to its stiffness in Stiff mode
// (cMarks).
// AC and IO are clobbered. Called via jsp.
taView,
    local rtn, vwNo, vwSet
    dap rtn
    lac i [mode:4]
    sas [MCONS]         // skip if the constraint mode
    jmp vwNo
    lac i [consType:4]
    sas [CTSTIFF]       // skip if Stiff's
    jmp vwNo
    law 1
    jmp vwSet
vwNo,
    cla
vwSet,
    sad roSt            // skip if the view changed
    jmp rtn
    dac roSt
    dzm taSnapE
    dzm roOK
    jsp roHide
    law 1
    dac taDue
    dac i [cMkDirty:010]
rtn, jmp .
    endloc

// The end of an analysis, its state and why, then the readouts written (taFin), then the count of
// analyses, and nothing more to do. With no Beam there are no readouts.
taOK,
    dzm taWhy
    law TAOK
    jmp taFin
taNone,
    law TANONE
    dac taState
    dzm taWhy
    jmp taEnd
taMech,
    law TAWMECH
    jmp taBad
taLarge,
    law TAWLARGE
    jmp taBad
taZero,
    law TAWZERO
    jmp taBad
taMany,
    law TAWMANY
taBad,
    dac taWhy
    law TABAD
    jmp taFin
taEnd,
    idx taGen
taStill,
    lac [taIdle:013]
    dac taPhase
taIdle,
    jmp i taRtn

// Go on to the phase at AC, now while the pass's time lasts, else at the next pass.
taGo,
    dac taPhase
taGoT,
    jsp taTime
    spa                 // skip once the pass's time is spent
    jmp i taPhase
    jmp i taRtn

// The same for a factorization term (taPFk), the clock read only every eighth. A term is short,
// so a pass may run up to seven terms past TRUSSMS.
taGo8,
    dac taPhase
    isp taG8            // skip on the eighth term since the clock was read
    jmp i taPhase
    law i 0d8
    dac taG8
    jmp taGoT
taG8, 0


// The map, cleared, then each Roller's point marked with its entry's address complemented, which
// is negative, and each Fix's point given the zero slot, so that a Fix wins over a Roller on one
// point, and the first Roller over a second. The last analysis' counts of unknowns and
// entries are cleared first, so that one which ends before the numbering reports none.
taPMap,
    local mpClr, mpLoop, mpRoll, mpPin, mpNext, mpDone, mpPt, mpRtn, mpE, mpN, mpW
    dzm taNU
    dzm taNP
    lac [taMap:015]
    dac mpW
    law i MAXPTS
    dac mpN
mpClr,
    dzm i mpW
    idx mpW
    isp mpN
    jmp mpClr
    lac [cEntries:011]
    dac mpE
    lac i [cCount:011]
    sza i               // skip if the table holds entries
    jmp mpDone
    cma
    dac mpN
mpLoop,
    lac i mpE
    sad [CTROLL]        // skip unless a Roller
    jmp mpRoll
    sad [CTF]           // skip unless a Fix
    jmp mpPin
mpNext,
    lac mpE
    add [CW]
    dac mpE
    isp mpN
    jmp mpLoop
mpDone,
    lac [taPJnt:013]
    jmp taGo
mpRoll,
    jsp mpPt
    lac i mpW
    sza                 // skip unless the point is marked already
    jmp mpNext
    lac mpE
    cma
    dac i mpW
    jmp mpNext
mpPin,
    jsp mpPt
    lac [taUX:013+TANJ]
    dac i mpW
    jmp mpNext

// mpW = the address of the map's word for the entry's point A.
// AC is clobbered, IO preserved. Called via jsp.
mpPt,
    dap mpRtn
    lac mpE
    add [1]
    dac mpW
    lac i mpW
    add [taMap:015]
    dac mpW
mpRtn, jmp .
mpE, 0
mpN, 0
mpW, 0
    endloc

// The joints. Each Beam is a member, its points and its parameter word, the stiffness (taMK),
// kept and its ends' addresses found (taJoin), which makes its points joints at their first
// naming and counts each joint's members (in its taUX word). No Beam means no truss. Then each
// joint's incidences are given their place, a word a member, their first's address in its taJI
// word and its fill pointer (in its taUX word), minus their count in its taJN word, and its
// members no more than TANI.
taPJnt,
    local jnLoop, jnNext, jnPlace, jnDone, jnE, jnN, jnW, jnA, jnI, jnR, jnF, jnC
    dzm taNM
    dzm taNJ
    lac [cEntries:011]
    dac jnE
    lac i [cCount:011]
    sza i               // skip if the table holds entries
    jmp taNone
    cma
    dac jnN
jnLoop,
    lac i jnE
    sas [CTBEAM]        // skip if a Beam
    jmp jnNext
    lac jnE
    add [1]
    dac jnW
    lac i jnW
    dac jnA
    lac taNM
    add [taMA:013]
    dac jnI
    lac jnA
    dac i jnI
    jda taJoin
    lac taNM
    add [taJA:013]
    dac jnI
    lac taJoin
    dac i jnI
    idx jnW
    lac i jnW
    dac jnA
    lac taNM
    add [taMB:013]
    dac jnI
    lac jnA
    dac i jnI
    jda taJoin
    lac taNM
    add [taJB:013]
    dac jnI
    lac taJoin
    dac i jnI
    lac jnE
    add [5]
    dac jnW
    lac taNM
    add [taMK:3]
    dac jnI
    lac i jnW
    dac i jnI
    idx taNM
jnNext,
    lac jnE
    add [CW]
    dac jnE
    isp jnN
    jmp jnLoop
    lac taNM
    sza i               // skip if a Beam was found
    jmp taNone
    lac [taInc:015]
    dac jnI
    lac [taUX:013]
    dac jnF
    dzm jnN
jnPlace,
    lac jnN
    sad taNJ            // skip while joints remain
    jmp jnDone
    lac i jnF
    dac jnC
    sub [TANI+1]
    sma                 // skip unless the joint's members are too many
    jmp taMany
    lac jnF
    add [2*(TANJ+1)]
    dac jnR
    lac jnI
    dac i jnR
    dac i jnF
    lac jnR
    add [TANJ+1]
    dac jnR
    lac jnC
    cma
    dac i jnR
    lac jnC
    add jnI
    dac jnI
    idx jnF
    idx jnN
    jmp jnPlace
jnDone,
    lac [taPLoad:013]
    jmp taGo
jnE, 0
jnN, 0
jnW, 0
jnA, 0
jnI, 0
jnR, 0
jnF, 0
jnC, 0
    endloc

// A member's end. A pin's is the zero slot; any other point is made a joint at its first
// naming, a roller if the map marked it so, and counted one member more in its taUX word.
// Entry AC = the point. Exit taJoin = the address of its horizontal displacement, or a roller's
// along its axis. AC and IO are clobbered. Called via jda taJoin.
taJoin, 0
    local rtn, jwOld, jwW, jwV, jwX
    dap rtn
    lac taJoin
    add [taMap:015]
    dac jwW
    lac i jwW
    dac taJoin
    sad [taUX:013+TANJ] // skip unless the point is a pin
    jmp rtn
    dac jwV
    sub [2]
    sma                 // skip if the point is no joint yet
    jmp jwOld
    lac taNJ
    sad [TANJ]          // skip unless the joints are too many
    jmp taMany
    add [taJR:013]
    dac jwX
    lac jwV
    dac i jwX
    lac taNJ
    add [taUX:013]
    dac i jwW
    dac taJoin
    dzm i taJoin
    idx taNJ
jwOld,
    idx i taJoin
rtn, jmp .
jwW, 0
jwV, 0
jwX, 0
    endloc

// The members' directions, a member at a time from taDM. A member of no length gives no answer
// (taZero). Its e = (dx, dy) / L goes to tdE, six words a member (e_x, then e_y), from taUnit.
// Each member is placed among its ends' incidences, but a pinned end's. Then the rollers' axes,
// from the first joint.
taPDir,
    local drAdd, drRtn, drDone, drA, drB, drW, drJ, drQ, drP, drE
    lac taDM
    sad taNM            // skip while members remain
    jmp drDone
    add [taMB:013]
    dac drW
    lac i drW
    dac drB
    lac taDM
    add [taMA:013]
    dac drW
    lac i drW
    dac drA
    add [pointX:3]
    dac drW
    lac drB
    add [pointX:3]
    dac drQ
    lac i drQ
    sub i drW
    dac taDD
    lac drA
    add [pointY:3]
    dac drW
    lac drB
    add [pointY:3]
    dac drQ
    lac i drQ
    sub i drW
    dac taDE
    ior taDD
    sza i               // skip if the member has a length
    jmp taZero
    lac taDM
    add taDM
    dac drE
    add drE
    add drE
    add [tdE:016]
    jda taUnit

    lac taDM
    add [taJA:013]
    dac drW
    lac i drW
    dac drA
    lac taDM
    add [taJB:013]
    dac drW
    lac i drW
    dac drB
    lac drA
    dac drJ
    lac drB
    jda drAdd
    lac drB
    dac drJ
    lac drA
    jda drAdd
    idx taDM
    lac [taPDir:013]
    jmp taGo
drDone,
    dzm taAJ
    lac [taPAxis:013]
    jmp taGo

// The member placed among the incidences of the end whose taUX word is at drJ, unless that is
// a pin's, at the fill pointer that word holds, as the other end's address (AC).
// AC and IO are clobbered. Called via jda drAdd.
drAdd, 0
    dap drRtn
    lac drJ
    sad [taUX:013+TANJ] // skip unless the end is a pin's
    jmp drRtn
    dac drQ
    lac i drQ
    dac drP
    lac drAdd
    dac i drP
    idx drP
    dac i drQ
drRtn, jmp .
drA, 0
drB, 0
drW, 0
drJ, 0
drQ, 0
drP, 0
drE, 0
    endloc
taDM, 0

// The unit vector of (taDD, taDE), not both 0, to the two numbers at the full address in AC and
// three words on. 1/L comes from a seed floor(2^31 / g) 2^-31 off taDir's root g of the vector
// as taDir doubled it, then one Newton step y (3 - x y^2) / 2, x the doubled vector's length
// squared, exact; the unit vector is the doubled vector times it. A member's direction (taPDir)
// and a roller's axis (taPAxis).
// AC and IO are clobbered; taDD and taDE are left doubled. Called via jda taUnit.
taUnit, 0
    local rtn, unE
    dap rtn
    lac taUnit
    dac unE
    jsp taDir

    // The seed, 2^31 / g (the dividend 2^31 is 2^32 in AC:IO, its high part under g).
    lac [040000]
    cli
    div taG
    cla                 // no skip is overflow, which a root of 2^15 or more cannot make
    jda fInt
    law i 0d31
    add faE
    dac faE
    lac [drY:3]
    jda faSt

    // x = dx^2 + dy^2.
    lac taDD
    jda fInt
    jsp fbFa
    jsp fMul
    lac [drX:3]
    jda faSt
    lac taDE
    jda fInt
    jsp fbFa
    jsp fMul
    lac [drX:3]
    jda fbLd
    jsp fAdd
    lac [drX:3]
    jda faSt

    // y (3 - x y y) / 2.
    lac [drY:3]
    jda faLd
    jsp fbFa
    jsp fMul
    lac [drX:3]
    jda fbLd
    jsp fMul
    jsp fNeg
    lac [0140000]
    lio [2]
    jda fbSet
    jsp fAdd
    lac [drY:3]
    jda fbLd
    jsp fMul
    law i 1
    add faE
    dac faE
    lac [drY:3]
    jda faSt

    // The vector times y.
    lac taDD
    jda fInt
    lac [drY:3]
    jda fbLd
    jsp fMul
    lac unE
    jda faSt
    lac taDE
    jda fInt
    lac [drY:3]
    jda fbLd
    jsp fMul
    lac unE
    add [3]
    jda faSt
rtn, jmp .
unE, 0
    endloc

// The rollers' axes, a joint a step from taAJ. Each roller joint's unit axis goes to its six
// words of taAX (bank 3), from the direction of the line its Roller entry names (taRlD); a level
// axis is (1, 0) exactly. Then the joints' order.
taPAxis,
    local axLevel, axNext, axDone, axP, axW
    lac taAJ
    sad taNJ            // skip while joints remain
    jmp axDone
    add [taJR:013]
    dac axP
    lac i axP
    sza i               // skip if a roller
    jmp axNext
    cma
    jda taRlD
    lac taAJ
    add taAJ
    dac axW
    add axW
    add axW
    add [taAX:3]
    dac axW
    lac rlX
    dac taDD
    lac rlY
    dac taDE
    sza i               // skip unless level
    jmp axLevel
    lac axW
    jda taUnit
    jmp axNext
axLevel,
    law 1
    jda fInt
    lac axW
    jda faSt
    lac axW
    add [3]
    dac axW
    dzm i axW
    idx axW
    dzm i axW
    idx axW
    dzm i axW
axNext,
    idx taAJ
    lac [taPAxis:013]
    jmp taGo
axDone,
    lac [taPOrd:013]
    jmp taGo

axP, 0
axW, 0
    endloc
taAJ, 0

// A roller's axis from the line its entry names, its B and C points, as the constraint module's
// cAxis finds it. (dx, dy) from B to C, turned to point right, or up when plumb, goes to rlX and
// rlY; (0, 0) when level, and for a level roller, B and C one point.
// Entry: AC = the entry's full address. AC and IO are clobbered. Called via jda taRlD.
taRlD, 0
    local rtn, rlTurn, rlNeg, rlB, rlC, rlT
    dap rtn
    lac taRlD
    add [2]
    dac rlT
    lac i rlT
    dac rlB
    idx rlT
    lac i rlT
    dac rlC
    add [pointX:3]
    dac rlT
    lac i rlT
    dac rlX
    lac rlB
    add [pointX:3]
    dac rlT
    lac rlX
    sub i rlT
    sad [0777777]       // skip unless -0
    cla
    dac rlX
    lac rlC
    add [pointY:3]
    dac rlT
    lac i rlT
    dac rlY
    lac rlB
    add [pointY:3]
    dac rlT
    lac rlY
    sub i rlT
    sad [0777777]       // skip unless -0
    cla
    dac rlY
    sza                 // skip if level
    jmp rlTurn
    dzm rlX
    jmp rtn
rlTurn,
    lac rlX
    spa                 // skip unless dx is negative
    jmp rlNeg
    sza                 // skip if dx is 0
    jmp rtn
    lac rlY
    sma                 // skip if dy is negative
    jmp rtn
rlNeg,
    lac rlX
    cma
    sad [0777777]       // skip unless -0
    cla
    dac rlX
    lac rlY
    cma
    dac rlY
rtn, jmp .
rlB, 0
rlC, 0
rlT, 0
    endloc
rlX, 0
rlY, 0

// Whether joint k is a roller on an axis not level, whose a_y is not zero. The result is the full
// address of its a_x in taAX, or 0 if it is not.
// Entry: AC = k. Exit: AC as said. IO is preserved. Called via jda taIncl.
taIncl, 0
    local rtn, tiNo, tiT
    dap rtn
    lac taIncl
    add [taJR:013]
    dac tiT
    lac i tiT
    sza i               // skip if a roller
    jmp tiNo
    lac taIncl
    add taIncl
    dac tiT
    add tiT
    add tiT
    add [taAX:3+4]
    dac tiT
    lac i tiT
    sza i               // skip if a_y is not 0; only zero has a high part of 0
    jmp tiNo
    lac tiT
    sub [4]
    jmp rtn
tiNo,
    cla
rtn, jmp .
tiT, 0
    endloc

// The root g (taG) of the vector (taDD, taDE), not both 0, which is left doubled until its
// larger part is 2^15 or more. Newton's root from the larger part plus half the smaller, four
// steps, kept no less than the larger. No division here can overflow (a square's high part is
// under 2^15, and the root is not under the larger part), so the no-skip words only fill their
// places.
// AC and IO are clobbered. Called via jsp.
taDir,
    local rtn, dvShift, dvRoot, dvStep, dvM, dvN, dvQ, dvI
    dap rtn
    lac taDD
    spa
    cma
    dac dvM
    lac taDE
    spa
    cma
    dac dvN
    sub dvM
    spa                 // skip if the vertical part is the larger
    jmp dvShift
    lac dvM
    lio dvN
    dac dvN
    dio dvM
dvShift,
    lac dvM
    sub [0100000]
    sma                 // skip while the larger part is under 2^15
    jmp dvRoot
    lac taDD
    sal 1s
    dac taDD
    lac taDE
    sal 1s
    dac taDE
    lac dvM
    sal 1s
    dac dvM
    lac dvN
    sal 1s
    dac dvN
    jmp dvShift
dvRoot,
    lac dvN
    sar 1s
    add dvM
    dac taG
    law i 4
    dac dvI
dvStep,
    lac taDD
    mul taDD
    div taG
    jmp taZero
    dac dvQ
    lac taDE
    mul taDE
    div taG
    jmp taZero
    add dvQ
    add taG             // under 2^18 as an unsigned number, and halved as one
    sar 1s
    and [0377777]
    dac taG
    isp dvI
    jmp dvStep
    lac taG
    sub dvM
    sma                 // skip if the root fell under the larger part
    jmp rtn
    lac dvM
    dac taG
rtn, jmp .
dvM, 0
dvN, 0
dvQ, 0
dvI, 0
    endloc
taDD, 0
taDE, 0
taG, 0

// The loads. Each Load's ten times its line's vector is added to its point A's sums (taFX and,
// TANJ after it, taFY) when A is a joint, an overflow too large (taLarge). Then the members'
// directions, from the first.
taPLoad,
    local ldClr, ldScan, ldLoop, ldNext, ldDone, ldTen, ldTRtn, ldE, ldN, ldW, ldA, ldB, ldX, \
        ldD
    dzm ldN
ldClr,
    lac ldN
    sad taNJ            // skip while joints remain
    jmp ldScan
    add [taFX:013]
    dac ldW
    dzm i ldW
    add [TANJ]
    dac ldW
    dzm i ldW
    idx ldN
    jmp ldClr
ldScan,
    lac [cEntries:011]
    dac ldE
    lac i [cCount:011]
    sza i               // skip if the table holds entries
    jmp ldDone
    cma
    dac ldN
    szo
    nop                 // the overflow flag cleared, since each sum tests it
ldLoop,
    lac i ldE
    sas [CTLOAD]        // skip if a Load
    jmp ldNext
    lac ldE
    add [1]
    dac ldW
    lac i ldW
    dac ldA
    idx ldW
    lac i ldW
    dac ldB
    lac ldA
    add [taMap:015]
    dac ldW
    lac i ldW
    sad [taUX:013+TANJ] // skip unless A is a pin
    jmp ldNext
    dac ldX
    sub [2]
    spa                 // skip if A is a joint
    jmp ldNext
    lac ldX
    sub [taUX:013]
    add [taFX:013]
    dac ldX
    lac ldA
    add [pointX:3]
    dac ldW
    lac ldB
    add [pointX:3]
    dac ldD
    lac i ldD
    sub i ldW
    jda ldTen
    add i ldX
    dac i ldX
    szo                 // skip unless the sum overflowed
    jmp taLarge
    lac ldX
    add [TANJ]
    dac ldX
    lac ldA
    add [pointY:3]
    dac ldW
    lac ldB
    add [pointY:3]
    dac ldD
    lac i ldD
    sub i ldW
    jda ldTen
    add i ldX
    dac i ldX
    szo                 // skip unless the sum overflowed
    jmp taLarge
ldNext,
    lac ldE
    add [CW]
    dac ldE
    isp ldN
    jmp ldLoop
ldDone,
    dzm taDM
    lac [taPDir:013]
    jmp taGo

// AC = ten times AC, a coordinates' difference.
// IO preserved. Called via jda ldTen.
ldTen, 0
    dap ldTRtn
    lac ldTen
    sal 2s
    add ldTen
    sal 1s
ldTRtn, jmp .
ldE, 0
ldN, 0
ldW, 0
ldA, 0
ldB, 0
ldX, 0
ldD, 0
    endloc

// The joints' order (taOrd), which numbers the unknowns (taPNum). It is breadth first from the
// first joint not yet reached with the fewest neighbors that are joints, each joint's neighbors
// in its incidences' order, then again from the next such joint until every joint is reached. A
// joint's taUY word marks it reached. Each start (taPOrS) is a step, and each joint taken from
// the queue (taPOrB).
taPOrd,
    local orClr, orGo, orScan, orDeg, orNext, orBest, orInc, orSkip, orDone, orAdd, oaRtn, orJ, \
        orP, orI, orC, orD, orO, orBJ, orBD, orHead, orTail
    dzm orJ
orClr,
    lac orJ
    sad taNJ            // skip while joints remain
    jmp orGo
    add [taUY:013]
    dac orP
    dzm i orP
    idx orJ
    jmp orClr
orGo,
    dzm orHead
    dzm orTail
    lac [taPOrS:013]
    jmp taGo
taPOrS,
    lac orTail
    sad taNJ            // skip while a joint is not reached
    jmp orDone
    lac [0377777]
    dac orBD
    lac [taUX:013]
    dac orJ
orScan,
    lac orJ
    sub [taUX:013]
    sad taNJ            // skip while joints remain
    jmp orBest
    lac orJ
    add [TANJ+1]
    dac orP
    lac i orP
    sza                 // skip unless reached
    jmp orNext

    // Its neighbors that are joints, its incidences whose other end is not a pin.
    lac orJ
    add [2*(TANJ+1)]
    dac orP
    lac i orP
    dac orI
    lac orP
    add [TANJ+1]
    dac orP
    lac i orP
    dac orC
    dzm orD
orDeg,
    lac i orI
    sas [taUX:013+TANJ] // skip if the other end is a pin
    idx orD
    idx orI
    isp orC
    jmp orDeg
    lac orD
    sub orBD
    sma                 // skip if fewer than the fewest so far
    jmp orNext
    add orBD
    dac orBD
    lac orJ
    dac orBJ
orNext,
    idx orJ
    jmp orScan
orBest,
    lac orBJ
    jda orAdd
    lac [taPOrB:013]
    jmp taGo
taPOrB,
    lac orHead
    sad orTail          // skip while the queue holds joints
    jmp taPOrS
    add [taOrd:013]
    dac orP
    idx orHead
    lac i orP
    add [2*(TANJ+1)]
    dac orP
    lac i orP
    dac orI
    lac orP
    add [TANJ+1]
    dac orP
    lac i orP
    dac orC
orInc,
    lac i orI
    sad [taUX:013+TANJ] // skip unless the other end is a pin
    jmp orSkip
    dac orO
    add [TANJ+1]
    dac orP
    lac i orP
    sza                 // skip unless reached
    jmp orSkip
    lac orO
    jda orAdd
orSkip,
    idx orI
    isp orC
    jmp orInc
    lac [taPOrB:013]
    jmp taGo
orDone,
    lac [taPNum:013]
    jmp taGo

// The joint whose taUX word is at AC marked reached, and put at the queue's end.
// AC is clobbered, IO preserved. Called via jda orAdd.
orAdd, 0
    dap oaRtn
    lac orAdd
    add [TANJ+1]
    dac orP
    law 1
    dac i orP
    lac orTail
    add [taOrd:013]
    dac orP
    lac orAdd
    dac i orP
    idx orTail
oaRtn, jmp .
orJ, 0
orP, 0
orI, 0
orC, 0
orD, 0
orO, 0
orBJ, 0
orBD, 0
orHead, 0
orTail, 0
    endloc

// The unknowns numbered in the reverse of taOrd. Each joint's horizontal displacement (a
// roller's along its axis), then, but for a roller, its vertical one, in its taUX and taUY
// words; a roller's taUY word, and the zero slot's two, -1. Then, a joint a step from taFJn
// (taPFst), its unknowns' first coupled unknown, the lowest of the joint's and its neighbors'
// (tdU's second word); then each row's base
// address (tdU's first), that of its column 0 were the row whole, the rows packed from tdK
// (taPBase). A profile past TAPROF entries is too many.
taPNum,
    local nuLoop, nuRoll, nuPin, nuQ, nuN, nuJ, nuP, nuR
    dzm nuN
    lac taNJ
    dac nuQ
nuLoop,
    lac nuQ
    sza i               // skip while joints remain
    jmp nuPin
    sub [1]
    dac nuQ
    add [taOrd:013]
    dac nuP
    lac i nuP
    dac nuJ
    lac nuN
    dac i nuJ
    idx nuN
    lac nuJ
    sub [taUX:013]
    add [taJR:013]
    dac nuP
    lac i nuP
    dac nuR
    lac nuJ
    add [TANJ+1]
    dac nuP
    lac nuR
    sza                 // skip unless a roller
    jmp nuRoll
    lac nuN
    dac i nuP
    idx nuN
    jmp nuLoop
nuRoll,
    law i 1
    dac i nuP
    jmp nuLoop
nuPin,
    law i 1
    dac i [taUX:013+TANJ]
    dac i [taUY:013+TANJ]
    lac nuN
    dac taNU
    lac [taUX:013]
    dac taFJn
    lac [taPFst:013]
    jmp taGo
nuQ, 0
nuN, 0
nuJ, 0
nuP, 0
nuR, 0
    endloc

taPFst,
    local fsInc, fsSkip, fsPut, fsRtn, fsLo, fsI, fsC, fsO, fsP, fsU
    lac taFJn
    sub [taUX:013]
    sad taNJ            // skip while joints remain
    jmp taPBase
    lac i taFJn
    dac fsLo
    lac taFJn
    add [2*(TANJ+1)]
    dac fsP
    lac i fsP
    dac fsI
    lac fsP
    add [TANJ+1]
    dac fsP
    lac i fsP
    dac fsC
fsInc,
    lac i fsI
    sad [taUX:013+TANJ] // skip unless the other end is a pin
    jmp fsSkip
    dac fsO
    lac i fsO
    sub fsLo
    sma                 // skip if the neighbor's unknown is the lower
    jmp fsSkip
    lac i fsO
    dac fsLo
fsSkip,
    idx fsI
    isp fsC
    jmp fsInc
    lac i taFJn
    jda fsPut
    lac taFJn
    add [TANJ+1]
    dac fsP
    lac i fsP
    sma                 // skip if the joint has no vertical unknown
    jda fsPut
    idx taFJn
    lac [taPFst:013]
    jmp taGo

// tdU's second word for unknown AC = fsLo.
// AC is clobbered, IO preserved. Called via jda fsPut.
fsPut, 0
    dap fsRtn
    lac fsPut
    add fsPut
    add [tdU:016+1]
    dac fsU
    lac fsLo
    dac i fsU
fsRtn, jmp .
fsLo, 0
fsI, 0
fsC, 0
fsO, 0
fsP, 0
fsU, 0
    endloc
taFJn, 0

taPBase,
    local bsLoop, bsDone, bsI, bsP, bsB, bsT, bsF
    dzm bsI
    dzm bsB
    lac [tdU:016]
    dac bsP
bsLoop,
    lac bsI
    sad taNU            // skip while rows remain
    jmp bsDone
    lac bsP
    add [1]
    dac bsT
    lac i bsT
    dac bsF
    lac bsB
    sub bsF
    dac bsT
    add bsT
    add bsT
    add [tdK:016]
    dac i bsP
    lac bsI
    sub bsF
    add [1]
    add bsB
    dac bsB
    lac bsP
    add [2]
    dac bsP
    idx bsI
    jmp bsLoop
bsDone,
    lac bsB
    dac taNP
    sub [TAPROF+1]
    sma                 // skip unless the profile is past its room
    jmp taMany
    lac [tdK:016]
    dac taZP
    lac bsB
    add bsB
    add bsB
    cma
    dac taZN
    lac [taPZero:013]
    jmp taGo
bsI, 0
bsP, 0
bsB, 0
bsT, 0
bsF, 0
    endloc

// The profile cleared, 256 words a step from taZP (taZN of them left, negated); then the right
// side (tdY), each joint's loads as numbers at its unknowns, a roller's on an axis not level
// f . a at its one.
taPZero,
    local zrLoop, zrMore, zrSide, zrJ, zrRoll, zrNext, zrDone, zrAt, zaRtn, zrC, zrK, zrP, zrU, \
        zrJp, zrA
    law i 0d256
    dac zrC
zrLoop,
    dzm i taZP
    idx taZP
    isp taZN            // skip once the profile is clear
    jmp zrMore
    jmp zrSide
zrMore,
    isp zrC             // skip once this step's words are clear
    jmp zrLoop
    lac [taPZero:013]
    jmp taGo
zrSide,
    dzm zrK
    lac [taUX:013]
    dac zrJp
zrJ,
    lac zrK
    sad taNJ            // skip while joints remain
    jmp zrDone
    add [taFX:013]
    dac zrP
    lac i zrP
    jda fInt
    lac zrK
    jda taIncl
    sza                 // skip unless a roller on an axis not level
    jmp zrRoll
    lac i zrJp
    jda zrAt
    jda faSt
    lac zrJp
    add [TANJ+1]
    dac zrP
    lac i zrP
    spa                 // skip if the joint has a vertical unknown
    jmp zrNext
    dac zrU
    lac zrK
    add [taFX:013+TANJ]
    dac zrP
    lac i zrP
    jda fInt
    lac zrU
    jda zrAt
    jda faSt
zrNext,
    idx zrJp
    idx zrK
    jmp zrJ

    // f_x a_x, FA holding f_x and AC a_x's address, then plus f_y a_y; a roller has no vertical
    // unknown.
zrRoll,
    dac zrA
    jda fbLd
    jsp fMul
    lac i zrJp
    jda zrAt
    dac zrU
    jda faSt
    lac zrK
    add [taFX:013+TANJ]
    dac zrP
    lac i zrP
    jda fInt
    lac zrA
    add [3]
    jda fbLd
    jsp fMul
    lac zrU
    jda fbLd
    jsp fAdd
    lac zrU
    jda faSt
    jmp zrNext
zrDone,
    dzm taAM
    lac [taPAsm:013]
    jmp taGo

// AC = the address of unknown AC's word in tdY.
// IO preserved. Called via jda zrAt.
zrAt, 0
    dap zaRtn
    lac zrAt
    add zrAt
    add zrAt
    add [tdY:016]
zaRtn, jmp .
zrC, 0
zrK, 0
zrP, 0
zrU, 0
zrJp, 0
zrA, 0
    endloc
taZP, 0
taZN, 0

// The matrix, a member at a time from taAM. Its coefficients c_A and c_B on its ends' first
// unknowns (asCo), kept in tdC for the forces, with taMI set when either is a roller's on an axis
// not level; then the six products of c_A, c_B and e_y (asPrT), added to each free end's block
// and taken from the coupling between its ends, at the ten places of asTab in its order. A member
// with no end on such a roller has c_A = c_B = e_x, and its products are e e^T's. A member whose
// stiffness k is not 1.0 has its six products multiplied by k (taKOf).
taPAsm,
    local asLoop, asPrL, asKL, asKDone, asDone, asPut, apGo, apRtn, asCo, acEx, acRtn, asE, asT, \
        asQ, asN, asI, asJ, asV, asM, asP, asOut, asIn
    lac taAM
    sad taNM            // skip while members remain
    jmp asDone
    add taAM
    dac asT
    add asT
    add asT
    dac asCA
    add [tdE:016]
    dac asE
    add [3]
    dac asEY
    lac asCA
    add [tdC:015]
    dac asCA
    add [3]
    dac asCB
    dzm asIn
    lac asCA
    dac asOut
    lac taAM
    add [taJA:013]
    dac asT
    lac i asT
    jda asCo
    lac asCB
    dac asOut
    lac taAM
    add [taJB:013]
    dac asT
    lac i asT
    jda asCo
    lac taAM
    add [taMI:3]
    dac asT
    lac asIn
    dac i asT

    // The six products, each asPrT row the addresses of the words holding its factors'
    // addresses, then the product's address.
    lac [asPrT:013]
    dac asQ
    law i 6
    dac asN
asPrL,
    lac i asQ
    dac asP
    lac i asP
    jda faLd
    idx asQ
    lac i asQ
    dac asP
    lac i asP
    jda fbLd
    idx asQ
    jsp fMul
    lac i asQ
    jda faSt
    idx asQ
    isp asN
    jmp asPrL

    // The member's stiffness, when not 1.0, on each product.
    lac taAM
    jda taKOf
    sza i               // skip if a stiffness not 1.0
    jmp asKDone
    lac [asP1:3]
    dac asQ
    law i 6
    dac asN
asKL,
    lac asQ
    jda faLd
    lac [taK:013]
    jda fbLd
    jsp fMul
    lac asQ
    jda faSt
    lac asQ
    add [3]
    dac asQ
    isp asN
    jmp asKL
asKDone,

    // Each end's unknowns, -1 for none (a pin's, or a roller's vertical).
    lac taAM
    add [taJA:013]
    dac asT
    lac i asT
    dac asT
    lac i asT
    dac asXA
    lac asT
    add [TANJ+1]
    dac asT
    lac i asT
    dac asYA
    lac taAM
    add [taJB:013]
    dac asT
    lac i asT
    dac asT
    lac i asT
    dac asXB
    lac asT
    add [TANJ+1]
    dac asT
    lac i asT
    dac asYB

    // The ten places, each asTab row the addresses of i's and j's words and of the number, then
    // 1 to take it away.
    lac [asTab:013]
    dac asQ
    law i 0d10
    dac asN
asLoop,
    lac i asQ
    dac asP
    lac i asP
    dac asI
    idx asQ
    lac i asQ
    dac asP
    lac i asP
    dac asJ
    idx asQ
    lac i asQ
    dac asV
    idx asQ
    lac i asQ
    dac asM
    idx asQ
    jsp asPut
    isp asN
    jmp asLoop
    idx taAM
    lac [taPAsm:013]
    jmp taGo
asDone,
    dzm taFI
    lac [taPFac:013]
    jmp taGo

// K[i][j] (i and j the unknowns asI and asJ, the larger the row) plus the number at asV, or
// less it when asM is 1; nothing when either is -1.
// AC and IO are clobbered. Called via jsp.
asPut,
    dap apRtn
    lac asI
    spa                 // skip if there is an unknown i
    jmp apRtn
    lac asJ
    spa                 // skip if there is an unknown j
    jmp apRtn
    lac asI
    sub asJ
    sma                 // skip if j is the larger
    jmp apGo
    lac asI
    lio asJ
    dac asJ
    dio asI
apGo,
    lac asI
    add asI
    add [tdU:016]
    dac asP
    lac asJ
    add asJ
    add asJ
    add i asP
    dac asP
    jda faLd
    lac asV
    jda fbLd
    lac asM
    sza                 // skip unless taken away
    jsp fbNeg
    jsp fAdd
    lac asP
    jda faSt
apRtn, jmp .
